Full function is `saveRecordEditor` (src/routes/roster/+page.svelte:1548-1724). Key excerpt, the create-turned-update / existing-record branch (lines 1652-1690):
```
if (fresh.state === 'none') {
    const dbEntityId = row.dbEntityId ?? currentDbEntityId;
    if (!dbEntityId) {
        throw new Error(`roster: cannot resolve the database entity id for member ${memberId}`);
    }
    await createMemberRecord(cfg, {
        dbEntityId,
        personId: row.personId,
        name: recordForm.name,
        phone: recordForm.phone,
        email: recordForm.email,
        birthdate: recordForm.birthdate,
        id_code: recordForm.id_code
    });
} else {
    // The record id comes from the FRESH read, never from the cached
    // lookup — on the create-turned-update path there is no cached id at
    // all. `recordEditorOriginal` is null there too, and the empty
    // baseline it falls back to makes the diff send exactly the non-empty
    // fields — the same set `createMemberRecord` would have sent, so a
    // field the admin left empty never overwrites a value this editor
    // never saw.
    const original = recordEditorOriginal ?? {
        name: '',
        phone: '',
        email: '',
        birthdate: '',
        id_code: ''
    };
    const changes: Partial<
        Pick<MemberRecord, 'name' | 'phone' | 'email' | 'birthdate' | 'id_code'>
    > = {};
    if (recordForm.name !== original.name) changes.name = recordForm.name;
    if (recordForm.phone !== original.phone) changes.phone = recordForm.phone;
    if (recordForm.email !== original.email) changes.email = recordForm.email;
    if (recordForm.birthdate !== original.birthdate) changes.birthdate = recordForm.birthdate;
    if (recordForm.id_code !== original.id_code) changes.id_code = recordForm.id_code;
    await updateMemberRecord(cfg, fresh.record._id, changes);
}
```
The `else` branch fires for `fresh.state === 'one'` (create-turned-update, the case #280 targets) AND ALSO would be reachable structurally for `fresh.state === 'damaged'` were it not intercepted earlier — but `damaged` is handled and returned at lines 1644-1651 before reaching this `if/else`, so in practice this `else` only runs for `state: 'one'`. The diff is computed field-by-field against `original` (real baseline when `recordEditorOriginal` was set at open time i.e. record pre-existed; empty-string baseline when it was null i.e. create-turned-update). Every field whose current `recordForm` value differs from `original` is included in `changes` and sent via `updateMemberRecord`. On the create-turned-update path with prefilled-but-untouched `name`/`email`: `original.name === ''` and `original.email === ''`, but `recordForm.name`/`recordForm.email` are the non-empty prefilled values — so `recordForm.name !== original.name` and `recordForm.email !== original.email` are both true, and BOTH prefilled fields get included in `changes` and sent to `updateMemberRecord`, even though the admin never typed into them. This is the exact overwrite issue #280 reports.

Defined at `src/routes/+page.svelte:4710-4712`:
```
const seasonCardCollapseDisabled = $derived(
	seasonManageOpen && (seriesRunUnfinished || eventConvertRunUnfinished)
);
```
Where (both also `$derived`): `seriesRunUnfinished = seriesCreateSubmitting || seriesCreateResume !== null` (`:4678`) and `eventConvertRunUnfinished = eventConvertSubmitting || eventConvertResume !== null` (`:4684`).

So the toggle is refused exactly when the panel is open AND (a bulk event-series create is in flight or stopped-but-not-resolved) OR (a bulk event-type conversion run is in flight or stopped-but-not-resolved). `closeSeasonManagePanel` re-checks the same `seriesRunUnfinished || eventConvertRunUnfinished` pair itself at `:2958` before actually collapsing (the disabled attribute and the handler both enforce it). Deliberately narrower than `anyCreateSubmitting` — an in-flight plain season/event create does NOT block the collapse, per the doc comment at `:4696-4699`.

An automatic collapse-on-success (issue #244 half 1) must gate on this same condition — equivalently, calling `closeSeasonManagePanel()` itself (which already enforces it) rather than setting `seasonManageOpen = false` directly is the safe implementation, since the event-create success path can run while the panel is showing a live series/conversion run and an auto-collapse that skipped this check could tear down the only visible 'N of M remaining' progress state.

Today, on a successful create, focus is restored to the season-management PANEL itself, not <body> and not the collapse/expand button. `restoreEventCreateFocus(origin)` called at `:4448` is defined `:3437-3441`:
```
function restoreEventCreateFocus(origin: 'panel' | null): void {
	tick().then(() => {
		if (origin === 'panel') seasonManagePanelEl?.focus();
	});
}
```
`eventCreateOrigin` is typed `'panel' | null` (`:3232`); every call to `openEventCreateForm` passes the literal `'panel'` (signature `function openEventCreateForm(origin: 'panel'): void` at `:3355`) — per the doc comment at `:3428-3436`, '#213 removed the page-level [+ Event], every open is PANEL-born', so `origin` is effectively always `'panel'` for a real create, meaning focus today always lands on `seasonManagePanelEl`.

Existing focus helpers on this page, for reuse:
- `restoreEventCreateFocus(origin)` — `:3437-3441` (focuses the panel, `tick()`-deferred).
- `closeSeasonManagePanel()`'s own focus restoration at `:2978`: `tick().then(() => seasonManageExpandEl?.focus());` — returns focus to the collapsed card's `season-card-expand` button (`bind:this={seasonManageExpandEl}` at `:5705`). This is the natural landing spot if the new auto-collapse routes through `closeSeasonManagePanel()` — but that function unconditionally focuses `seasonManageExpandEl`, so if it fires alongside/after `restoreEventCreateFocus`'s panel-focus, ordering on the microtask queue decides which wins; the issue's 'gear-successor or the created event's agenda row' requirement means this ordering needs deliberate handling, not just calling both helpers back-to-back.
- The `$effect` at `:2989-2991` re-focuses `seasonManagePanelEl` whenever `seasonManageOpen` is true and the element exists.

No existing helper focuses an agenda ROW (the issue's other named target, 'the created event's agenda row') — no `data-testid`/element-ref for a just-created agenda row was found in this file, so that would be new code for half 1 (or shared with half 2's row-highlight work).
